[{:db/id 17592186192765 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-4c5afa8a-a09e-5d94-9d6f-17bde8db6cd3"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-4c5afa8a-a09e-5d94-9d6f-17bde8db6cd3" :question/id #uuid "4c5afa8a-a09e-5d94-9d6f-17bde8db6cd3" :question/math-academy-id "q-105422" :question/problem "Which of the following sets are neither open nor closed?\n\n- ${(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,2\\le x\\le 4,\\,0<{y}^{2}\\le 5}$\n- ${(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}<7}$\n- ${(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,1\\le x<4,\\,{y}^{2}<9}$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that:\n\n- A set is *open* if it does not contain any of its boundary points. In other words, an open set consists only of the interior points of the set.\n\n- A set is *closed* if it contains **all** of its boundary points. In other words, a closed set consists of all the interior and all the boundary points of the set.\n\nLet's examine our sets in turn.\n\n- The first set is *neither open nor closed*. It contains some of its boundary points, for example, the point $(2,\\sqrt{5}).$ On the other hand, it does not contain some other boundary points, for example, the point $(3,0).$\n\n- The second set is *open* since it doesn't contain any of its boundary points (the corresponding inequality is strict).\n\n- The third set is *neither open nor closed*. It contains some of its boundary points, for example, the point $(1,0).$ On the other hand, it does not contain some other boundary points, for example, the point $(4,0).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-0677d12a-c058-55e0-b0e6-dbd13fd6e32a"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-0677d12a-c058-55e0-b0e6-dbd13fd6e32a" :answer-field/id #uuid "0677d12a-c058-55e0-b0e6-dbd13fd6e32a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-4f20ef63-3480-55f7-95e5-2cc853da0048" :answer-field/choices ["answer-3fc08d88-96fa-5f9d-8557-7fd8fe262961" "answer-4f20ef63-3480-55f7-95e5-2cc853da0048" "answer-573b7e2b-ff52-5029-b107-d0355f51c237" "answer-a9dc495a-c9d0-52b6-b7d2-7e013a5139c5" "answer-846d05a9-d44d-5e50-8190-0ce86e7971a4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3fc08d88-96fa-5f9d-8557-7fd8fe262961" :answer/id #uuid "3fc08d88-96fa-5f9d-8557-7fd8fe262961" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4f20ef63-3480-55f7-95e5-2cc853da0048" :answer/id #uuid "4f20ef63-3480-55f7-95e5-2cc853da0048" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-573b7e2b-ff52-5029-b107-d0355f51c237" :answer/id #uuid "573b7e2b-ff52-5029-b107-d0355f51c237" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a9dc495a-c9d0-52b6-b7d2-7e013a5139c5" :answer/id #uuid "a9dc495a-c9d0-52b6-b7d2-7e013a5139c5" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-846d05a9-d44d-5e50-8190-0ce86e7971a4" :answer/id #uuid "846d05a9-d44d-5e50-8190-0ce86e7971a4" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186192767 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-b04f2bd5-de84-5515-a0a5-3d6c81e3d583"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-b04f2bd5-de84-5515-a0a5-3d6c81e3d583" :question/id #uuid "b04f2bd5-de84-5515-a0a5-3d6c81e3d583" :question/math-academy-id "q-161644" :question/problem "Which of the following sets are open?\n\n- ${(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}:\\text{ }-2\\le x\\le 0,\\,1\\le y\\le 2-x}$\n- ${(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}:\\text{ }-1<x<1,\\,0<y<1+x}$\n- ${(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}:\\text{ }4\\le {x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\le 9}$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that:\n\n- A set is *open* if it does not contain any of its boundary points. In other words, an open set consists only of the interior points of the set.\n\n- A set is *closed* if it contains **all** of its boundary points. In other words, a closed set consists of all the interior and all the boundary points of the set.\n\nLet's examine our sets in turn.\n\n- The first set is *closed* since it contains all of its boundary points (all the corresponding inequalities are not strict).\n\n- The second set is *open* since it doesn't contain any of its boundary points (all the corresponding inequalities are strict).\n\n- The third set is *closed* since it contains all of its boundary points (all the corresponding inequalities are not strict).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-6c28df82-226c-551a-9267-de3801bebac5"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-6c28df82-226c-551a-9267-de3801bebac5" :answer-field/id #uuid "6c28df82-226c-551a-9267-de3801bebac5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-0dbcbe48-2124-5037-bac0-c99498ef9fe0" :answer-field/choices ["answer-6e671489-f5be-562e-8530-e27db89c1e00" "answer-3a63ced9-ca36-5f7e-b7b0-e658c1fa60dd" "answer-408a94f7-529c-5ff0-8b23-26d97a71b99c" "answer-bcc31443-e5f9-544a-84d7-9325a05e998e" "answer-0dbcbe48-2124-5037-bac0-c99498ef9fe0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6e671489-f5be-562e-8530-e27db89c1e00" :answer/id #uuid "6e671489-f5be-562e-8530-e27db89c1e00" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3a63ced9-ca36-5f7e-b7b0-e658c1fa60dd" :answer/id #uuid "3a63ced9-ca36-5f7e-b7b0-e658c1fa60dd" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-408a94f7-529c-5ff0-8b23-26d97a71b99c" :answer/id #uuid "408a94f7-529c-5ff0-8b23-26d97a71b99c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bcc31443-e5f9-544a-84d7-9325a